requirements:
Wired specimens must satisfy mechanical limits based on condition:
a) Annealed (O) condition: High ductility and flexibility, with an elongation at break of at least 35 to 40 percent;
b) Hard-drawn (HD) condition: High tensile strength to withstand high-speed spooling and structural mechanical loading.

For quality audit inspections under Scheme-I, random samples must be drawn as per Table 1 (Levels of Control):
- Physical testing: 6-meter sample length;
- Chemical analysis: 5 pieces of 5 cm length.
